1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:01,867
<i>First, find out
what her interests are.</i>

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:02,900
<i> What does she like?</i>

3
00:00:03,033 --> 00:00:04,267
<i> She likes action movies.</i>

4
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:05,867
<i> Just like Joey.</i>

5
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,633
<i>Is that the reason
you came back here, Peter?</i>

6
00:00:07,767 --> 00:00:08,867
<i>Is she the one
you're trying to forget?</i>

7
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:10,667
<i>- May I buy something?
- What is it?</i>

8
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:11,833
<i> Four shampoos.</i>

9
00:00:11,967 --> 00:00:13,067
<i> What are you laughing at?</i>

10
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:15,667
<i>Well, Peter is teaching me
how to impress girls.</i>

11
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:16,800
<i> Idiot.</i>

12
00:00:16,933 --> 00:00:19,433
<i>You're trying to impress
our customer too?</i>

13
00:00:19,567 --> 00:00:20,500
<i> I was just testing it.</i>

14
00:00:20,633 --> 00:00:22,133
<i> It does looks effective.</i>

15
00:00:22,267 --> 00:00:23,367
<i> Why are we stopping?</i>

16
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:25,033
<i>Ma'am, looks like
we've got a flat tire.</i>

17
00:00:25,167 --> 00:00:26,233
<i> Our spare is broken.</i>

18
00:00:26,367 --> 00:00:27,433
<i> I haven't had it fixed yet.</i>

19
00:00:27,567 --> 00:00:28,467
<i> Stupid!</i>

20
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:29,767
<i> Berdugo is on his way.</i>

21
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:32,300
<i> He'll arrive early morning.</i>

22
00:00:32,433 --> 00:00:33,233
<i> Everything is ready.</i>

23
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:34,433
<i> Do you still love her?</i>

24
00:00:34,567 --> 00:00:36,433
<i>Actually, I love someone else
already...</i>

25
00:00:36,567 --> 00:00:37,733
<i> Friends like you.</i>

26
00:00:37,867 --> 00:00:38,933
<i> You love me already?</i>

27
00:00:39,067 --> 00:00:41,133
<i> But aren't we just pretending?</i>

28
00:00:41,267 --> 00:00:42,600
<i> There are some things...</i>

29
00:00:42,733 --> 00:00:44,667
<i> you can't fake, Joey.</i>

30
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:47,000
<i>Is that why you're here
in Valmora, to forget?</i>

31
00:00:47,133 --> 00:00:48,500
<i> That's the plan,</i>

32
00:00:48,633 --> 00:00:50,667
<i>but it feels like
I can't escape it.</i>

33
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:52,067
<i> The two are gone.</i>

34
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:54,233
<i> Where's Andrew?</i>

35
00:00:54,367 --> 00:00:56,900
<i>Even though my ex and I broke up
a long time ago,</i>

36
00:00:57,033 --> 00:00:58,000
<i> it's hard to recover.</i>

37
00:00:58,133 --> 00:00:59,567
<i>Tell me, are you
and Joey a couple?</i>

38
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:01,533
<i>Because I feel like
you're provoking me.</i>

39
00:01:01,667 --> 00:01:03,100
<i> You're too close to Joey,</i>

40
00:01:03,233 --> 00:01:05,133
<i>and I know you're doing it
to make me jealous.</i>

41
00:01:05,267 --> 00:01:07,000
<i>- We're done, aren't we?
- I know.</i>

42
00:01:07,167 --> 00:01:08,733
<i>I was the one who left,
the one who walked away,</i>

43
00:01:08,867 --> 00:01:10,167
<i> and I regret it.</i>

44
00:01:10,300 --> 00:01:12,667
<i>That's why I want you back,
Andrew.</i>

45
00:01:16,367 --> 00:01:18,633
<i> [OBB]</i>

46
00:01:33,900 --> 00:01:35,200
Joey...

47
00:01:35,333 --> 00:01:39,467
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

48
00:01:43,967 --> 00:01:47,400
Sorry, I feel embarrassed.

49
00:01:47,533 --> 00:01:48,733
I disturbed you.

50
00:01:48,867 --> 00:01:51,667
I thought something
bad happened to you.

51
00:01:52,767 --> 00:01:54,467
You don't have to say sorry,
okay?

52
00:01:56,367 --> 00:01:57,700
Yeah, that's true.

53
00:01:58,500 --> 00:02:00,300
You have nothing
to do with this.

54
00:02:00,733 --> 00:02:02,533
It's between me and Andrew.

55
00:02:03,133 --> 00:02:07,133
[HEAVY MUSIC CONTINUES]

56
00:02:23,767 --> 00:02:27,800
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

57
00:02:30,300 --> 00:02:32,200
I'll see you tomorrow, Clarissa?

58
00:02:33,667 --> 00:02:35,633
- All right.
- Okay.

59
00:02:35,767 --> 00:02:37,800
I'll just accompany mom
to her room.

60
00:02:40,633 --> 00:02:41,767
I like her.

61
00:02:41,900 --> 00:02:44,300
I hope she doesn't
give up easily.

62
00:02:44,433 --> 00:02:46,133
Then be nice to her.

63
00:02:46,733 --> 00:02:50,700
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

64
00:02:59,733 --> 00:03:03,967
[PHONE RINGING]

65
00:03:06,867 --> 00:03:09,033
<i>I'm sorry.
The subscriber...</i>

66
00:03:11,967 --> 00:03:12,967
Clarissa...

67
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:15,300
Amazing.

68
00:03:15,900 --> 00:03:17,833
Mom liked you.

69
00:03:17,967 --> 00:03:21,767
You know, she wasn't like that
with her past caregivers.

70
00:03:21,933 --> 00:03:24,033
Thank you, Ma'am.

71
00:03:25,367 --> 00:03:27,467
Oh, what's wrong?

72
00:03:28,100 --> 00:03:33,867
I was calling Joey
to share the good news.

73
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:36,400
But she's not answering
her phone.

74
00:03:36,533 --> 00:03:38,767
Maybe she fell asleep.

75
00:03:38,900 --> 00:03:40,533
It's already late anyway.

76
00:03:40,667 --> 00:03:42,533
I'm sure when you talk to her,

77
00:03:42,667 --> 00:03:44,900
she'll be happy about your news.

78
00:03:46,700 --> 00:03:49,300
Everything's going to be okay,
Clarissa,

79
00:03:49,433 --> 00:03:52,267
even your husband's situation.

80
00:03:53,133 --> 00:03:54,400
Just have faith.

81
00:03:54,567 --> 00:03:56,367
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

82
00:03:56,500 --> 00:03:57,533
Yes, Ma'am.

83
00:03:59,633 --> 00:04:00,733
[DOOR CLOSES]

84
00:04:00,867 --> 00:04:04,467
[ENGINE REVVING]

85
00:04:04,833 --> 00:04:09,033
[DAUNTING MUSIC PLAYING]

86
00:04:38,833 --> 00:04:39,700
Hey!

87
00:04:40,533 --> 00:04:42,167
What are you looking at?

88
00:04:42,300 --> 00:04:45,433
Bro, looks like he wants
to beat us to the plan.

89
00:04:45,567 --> 00:04:47,500
I don't intend to steal this.

90
00:04:47,633 --> 00:04:49,667
I just want to know whose car
this is.

91
00:04:49,800 --> 00:04:51,100
Idiot!

92
00:04:51,233 --> 00:04:53,067
Are you trying to fool us?

93
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:54,167
Wait, Man.

94
00:04:54,300 --> 00:04:55,467
I don't want trouble.

95
00:04:55,933 --> 00:04:57,300
I have a family.

96
00:04:57,433 --> 00:04:59,133
If you want to steal this car,

97
00:04:59,267 --> 00:05:00,167
it's yours.

98
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:01,300
Enough talk!

99
00:05:01,467 --> 00:05:03,067
Come on, hit him!

100
00:05:04,433 --> 00:05:07,733
Yes, I have nothing to do
with your real relationship.

101
00:05:07,867 --> 00:05:08,767
Joey...

102
00:05:08,900 --> 00:05:09,700
Wait.

103
00:05:11,300 --> 00:05:13,067
Are you jealous?

104
00:05:13,200 --> 00:05:14,400
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

105
00:05:14,533 --> 00:05:16,367
You and Andrew aren't together,
right?

106
00:05:17,300 --> 00:05:20,233
Or are you starting to have
feelings for Andrew?

107
00:05:22,067 --> 00:05:23,800
Me, jealous?

108
00:05:23,933 --> 00:05:25,167
No way.

109
00:05:25,300 --> 00:05:27,733
We're just pretending.

110
00:05:27,867 --> 00:05:29,700
Andrew and I are just friends.

111
00:05:30,800 --> 00:05:32,067
Well...
[CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY]

112
00:05:33,033 --> 00:05:34,367
That's good.

113
00:05:34,867 --> 00:05:36,033
That's good to know.

114
00:05:36,567 --> 00:05:39,067
I just don't want anyone
to get hurt.

115
00:05:39,967 --> 00:05:41,533
Especially now, it looks like...

116
00:05:41,667 --> 00:05:45,000
Andrew and I have a chance
to fix our relationship.

117
00:05:46,800 --> 00:05:49,400
I'm happy to hear that.

118
00:05:50,800 --> 00:05:52,433
Don't worry about me.

119
00:05:52,567 --> 00:05:54,600
I'm glad that you'll get back
together.

120
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:58,800
I'll go ahead
so you can talk more.

121
00:06:00,333 --> 00:06:01,633
Good luck to both of you.

122
00:06:02,467 --> 00:06:06,500
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

123
00:06:20,433 --> 00:06:24,133
[STIRRING EMOTIONAL
MUSIC CONTINUES]

124
00:06:24,267 --> 00:06:25,567
Andrew...

125
00:06:26,767 --> 00:06:28,500
where were we?

126
00:06:31,933 --> 00:06:33,367
Can we...

127
00:06:33,500 --> 00:06:35,267
Let's talk about this later.

128
00:06:36,600 --> 00:06:40,100
Our objective on why we're here
is more important.

129
00:06:41,533 --> 00:06:43,000
Someone might see us.

130
00:06:43,433 --> 00:06:47,400
[STIRRING EMOTIONAL
MUSIC CONTINUES]

131
00:07:01,467 --> 00:07:05,667
[DAUNTING MUSIC PLAYING]

132
00:07:15,133 --> 00:07:17,067
What are you doing?

133
00:07:17,200 --> 00:07:21,633
[DAUNTING MUSIC CONTINUES]

134
00:07:21,767 --> 00:07:22,700
- [EXCLAIMS]
- [INTENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

135
00:07:22,833 --> 00:07:24,533
[THUDS]

136
00:07:24,667 --> 00:07:25,900
[THUDS]

137
00:07:27,133 --> 00:07:28,433
[THUDS]

138
00:07:28,567 --> 00:07:29,733
[EXCLAIMS]

139
00:07:29,867 --> 00:07:31,533
[THUDS]

140
00:07:31,667 --> 00:07:32,867
I said I don't want trouble!
[DAUNTING MUSIC PLAYING]

141
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:34,600
Boss, please don't kill us!

142
00:07:34,733 --> 00:07:36,900
- Have mercy, Boss!
- Have some pity on us!

143
00:07:38,867 --> 00:07:39,867
Here's the cellphone!

144
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:41,633
That's all we stole!

145
00:07:41,767 --> 00:07:43,767
Just don't kill us, Boss!

146
00:07:43,900 --> 00:07:46,067
I don't want to see
your faces here again, got it?

147
00:07:46,200 --> 00:07:48,200
Yes, Boss! Let's go, Bro!

148
00:07:48,367 --> 00:07:52,600
[INTENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

149
00:08:02,733 --> 00:08:05,067
My companion got lost so...

150
00:08:05,200 --> 00:08:06,367
I was going to bring this
to the room.

151
00:08:06,500 --> 00:08:08,767
I'll return it to him.

152
00:08:09,667 --> 00:08:10,900
I thought you left me.

153
00:08:12,067 --> 00:08:13,300
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

154
00:08:13,433 --> 00:08:15,100
You were on the phone
for a long time.

155
00:08:15,233 --> 00:08:16,300
I walked around.

156
00:08:16,433 --> 00:08:18,567
And I think, you know what?
I'm getting drunk.

157
00:08:18,700 --> 00:08:19,667
[CHUCKLES]

158
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:21,100
Are you trying to get me drunk?

159
00:08:21,533 --> 00:08:23,533
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

160
00:08:23,667 --> 00:08:24,833
Just kidding.

161
00:08:24,967 --> 00:08:26,633
I'm just kidding.
[CHUCKLES]

162
00:08:28,867 --> 00:08:30,500
Excuse me,

163
00:08:30,633 --> 00:08:32,933
I think I'm the one who's drunk.

164
00:08:33,867 --> 00:08:35,067
I'm going to bed now.
Good night.

165
00:08:37,500 --> 00:08:41,633
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

166
00:08:45,733 --> 00:08:47,800
Actually, me too...

167
00:08:48,400 --> 00:08:50,300
I still have boyfriend duties.

168
00:08:55,500 --> 00:08:57,200
I need to clean up my stuff.

169
00:08:57,900 --> 00:09:02,067
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

170
00:09:18,733 --> 00:09:21,133
Oh, I don't have a key.

171
00:09:21,867 --> 00:09:23,667
So annoying!

172
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:28,000
[GLUM MUSIC PLAYING]

173
00:09:49,567 --> 00:09:51,267
[ZOEY CHUCKLES]

174
00:09:51,400 --> 00:09:52,700
You looked so sad earlier

175
00:09:52,833 --> 00:09:54,433
when you were telling the story
about your ex.

176
00:09:54,867 --> 00:09:58,033
But now, you can't wipe
the smile off your face.

177
00:09:58,167 --> 00:09:59,967
I'm just happy I enjoyed
our date

178
00:10:00,100 --> 00:10:01,967
under the stars.

179
00:10:03,933 --> 00:10:05,033
Wait...

180
00:10:05,867 --> 00:10:08,300
Maybe you're already
bored with me?

181
00:10:09,567 --> 00:10:10,433
No.

182
00:10:11,033 --> 00:10:12,267
I'm enjoying this too.

183
00:10:12,600 --> 00:10:14,133
And this is my plan...

184
00:10:14,267 --> 00:10:16,100
to have a good business,

185
00:10:16,833 --> 00:10:18,767
so I won't have
to worry about money.

186
00:10:18,900 --> 00:10:22,167
Just relax, because working all
the time is exhausting.

187
00:10:22,833 --> 00:10:24,533
Speaking of work...

188
00:10:25,533 --> 00:10:26,833
I have a question for you.

189
00:10:26,967 --> 00:10:28,033
What is it?

190
00:10:29,033 --> 00:10:33,100
Didn't you say
you own this resort,

191
00:10:33,233 --> 00:10:35,933
but then your boss called you?

192
00:10:36,700 --> 00:10:38,200
What's that? A different job?

193
00:10:38,333 --> 00:10:39,867
Something like that.

194
00:10:40,667 --> 00:10:42,333
What kind of work
do you do for him?

195
00:10:57,133 --> 00:10:58,800
What are you doing here?

196
00:11:03,133 --> 00:11:05,067
I don't have a key.

197
00:11:09,567 --> 00:11:10,567
Key.

198
00:11:14,333 --> 00:11:18,567
[LIGHT PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

199
00:11:20,500 --> 00:11:23,633
Can I talk to you?

200
00:11:25,033 --> 00:11:27,600
I just want to explain
something.

201
00:11:29,900 --> 00:11:32,400
Explain what?
There's nothing to explain.

202
00:11:34,400 --> 00:11:35,933
Just don't give me false hope.

203
00:11:36,067 --> 00:11:37,833
It's frustrating.

204
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:42,333
Give you false hope?

205
00:11:42,700 --> 00:11:44,300
[PLEASANT MUSIC PLAYING]

206
00:11:44,433 --> 00:11:45,967
It's about the key!

207
00:11:46,633 --> 00:11:48,600
I thought you were going
to give it to me.

208
00:11:49,300 --> 00:11:51,800
But you don't want to,
you're just making me wait.

209
00:11:52,467 --> 00:11:53,767
I want to go inside already.

210
00:11:53,900 --> 00:11:55,200
I'm getting tired.

211
00:11:57,467 --> 00:11:58,833
Okay, listen to me.

212
00:12:01,400 --> 00:12:03,433
I didn't know...

213
00:12:04,900 --> 00:12:07,067
Zoey would do that.

214
00:12:09,400 --> 00:12:10,700
I'm sorry.

215
00:12:12,600 --> 00:12:13,733
Why are you apologizing?

216
00:12:13,867 --> 00:12:15,667
You don't need to.

217
00:12:16,400 --> 00:12:18,667
If you're getting back together,

218
00:12:18,967 --> 00:12:20,467
then go ahead.

219
00:12:21,200 --> 00:12:22,933
Right? If that makes you happy.

220
00:12:23,367 --> 00:12:27,367
But that's not part of my plan.

221
00:12:27,500 --> 00:12:29,500
Still, it could happen.

222
00:12:31,400 --> 00:12:32,267
Right?

223
00:12:34,233 --> 00:12:35,833
Why do you...

224
00:12:37,400 --> 00:12:38,833
seem upset?

225
00:12:39,300 --> 00:12:42,500
Maybe because I expected you
to be honest.

226
00:12:44,367 --> 00:12:47,333
That you'll admit you still have
feelings for her.

227
00:12:48,067 --> 00:12:50,333
But earlier you kept denying it.

228
00:12:51,833 --> 00:12:53,667
You said you didn't.

229
00:12:54,233 --> 00:12:57,067
But that's the truth.

230
00:12:59,400 --> 00:13:00,967
I like someone else.

231
00:13:04,100 --> 00:13:08,067
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

232
00:13:08,200 --> 00:13:10,833
You seem suddenly interested
in my work.

233
00:13:10,967 --> 00:13:12,400
[CHUCKLES]
Nothing.

234
00:13:12,533 --> 00:13:14,767
I'm just asking,
I'm just curious.

235
00:13:15,600 --> 00:13:18,733
Maybe I can apply for a job
to your boss?

236
00:13:19,700 --> 00:13:22,000
Or why don't you just
apply to me?

237
00:13:22,167 --> 00:13:23,600
I'd hire you right away.

238
00:13:23,733 --> 00:13:25,000
[SNICKERS]
What?

239
00:13:25,133 --> 00:13:27,300
I could even make you
my personal assistant.

240
00:13:28,100 --> 00:13:29,333
No, not with you.

241
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:32,800
We might end up with
a conflict of interest.

242
00:13:33,900 --> 00:13:35,833
Better with your boss.

243
00:13:36,300 --> 00:13:38,933
Right? Think about it.
What if I get in?

244
00:13:39,067 --> 00:13:41,500
I might stay here
in Valmora for good.

245
00:13:44,367 --> 00:13:45,500
Please.

246
00:13:46,133 --> 00:13:47,567
Introduce me to him.

247
00:13:47,700 --> 00:13:49,867
Because if I get in,

248
00:13:50,800 --> 00:13:52,767
we'll be together longer.

249
00:13:52,900 --> 00:13:53,900
All right, all right.

250
00:13:54,033 --> 00:13:56,433
Tomorrow, I'll introduce you
to him.

251
00:13:56,600 --> 00:13:57,833
For real?

252
00:13:57,967 --> 00:14:00,167
[CHUCKLES]
Okay.

253
00:14:00,300 --> 00:14:01,300
Cheers!

254
00:14:02,133 --> 00:14:03,433
[CLINKS]

255
00:14:03,567 --> 00:14:08,100
[DAUNTING MUSIC CONTINUES]

256
00:14:08,233 --> 00:14:09,733
<i> There you are!</i>

257
00:14:09,867 --> 00:14:12,267
How are my two love birds?

258
00:14:14,267 --> 00:14:15,733
Auntie...

259
00:14:15,867 --> 00:14:17,300
How's your dinner?

260
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:19,067
Really good.

261
00:14:19,200 --> 00:14:21,133
Unique in a good way.

262
00:14:22,467 --> 00:14:24,433
My boyfriend, Andrew,
really enjoyed it.

263
00:14:24,567 --> 00:14:27,233
It even reached the other tent.

264
00:14:28,233 --> 00:14:35,867
[DAUNTING MUSIC CONTINUES]

265
00:14:36,367 --> 00:14:38,267
It's a pity I didn't catch you.

266
00:14:38,400 --> 00:14:43,600
I even rushed because I really
wanted to hear your love story,

267
00:14:43,733 --> 00:14:45,633
on how you met.

268
00:14:45,767 --> 00:14:46,733
But, Auntie...

269
00:14:47,300 --> 00:14:48,767
we're not leaving yet.

270
00:14:48,900 --> 00:14:50,000
[DAUNTING MUSIC PLAYING]

271
00:14:50,133 --> 00:14:53,433
What if we return the favor?

272
00:14:53,567 --> 00:14:54,967
We'll treat you to dinner.

273
00:14:56,100 --> 00:15:00,033
Oh, that's so sweet, dear,
but I have to decline.

274
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:03,133
Why? Are you leaving?

275
00:15:03,267 --> 00:15:04,300
No, dear, because...

276
00:15:04,433 --> 00:15:07,200
I have a very important meeting
tomorrow night,

277
00:15:07,333 --> 00:15:10,500
and this meeting could expand
my business.

278
00:15:10,633 --> 00:15:11,933
You know,

279
00:15:12,067 --> 00:15:14,633
my beauty is high maintenance.

280
00:15:14,767 --> 00:15:16,333
[CHUCKLES]

281
00:15:16,467 --> 00:15:17,333
Yes.

282
00:15:17,467 --> 00:15:18,733
[CHUCKLES]

283
00:15:18,867 --> 00:15:20,900
Oh, my god.

284
00:15:22,100 --> 00:15:24,067
The wine's all gone.
Can we order more?

285
00:15:24,200 --> 00:15:25,900
[PHONE RINGING]

286
00:15:26,033 --> 00:15:28,667
Oh, we could get another one,

287
00:15:28,800 --> 00:15:31,100
but I might not be able
to join you.

288
00:15:31,667 --> 00:15:33,667
What? Why?

289
00:15:33,800 --> 00:15:35,233
I have something I need to do.

290
00:15:36,900 --> 00:15:38,733
You're leaving me here alone?

291
00:15:39,767 --> 00:15:41,300
Can I come with you?

292
00:15:41,433 --> 00:15:43,100
Oh, how about this...

293
00:15:43,233 --> 00:15:47,033
get another wine,
I'll just call Madam Delilah.

294
00:15:47,167 --> 00:15:48,667
Then I'll come back, promise.

295
00:15:50,100 --> 00:15:50,967
Don't bother.

296
00:15:51,100 --> 00:15:52,700
I'll just go back to my room.

297
00:15:54,400 --> 00:15:55,933
Wait, don't be mad.

298
00:15:56,433 --> 00:15:57,967
You're not checking out yet,
right?

299
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:00,500
Okay, fine, how about this.

300
00:16:00,633 --> 00:16:02,300
If you can't wait for me
later tonight,

301
00:16:02,433 --> 00:16:05,700
let's meet again tomorrow?
[DAUNTING MUSIC PLAYING]

302
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:07,733
We'll have another date,
but different.

303
00:16:07,900 --> 00:16:09,233
More romantic.

304
00:16:10,233 --> 00:16:12,400
And then you'll leave me again?

305
00:16:12,533 --> 00:16:13,600
No, not anymore.

306
00:16:14,233 --> 00:16:17,100
Besides, I'm going to introduce
you to my boss, right?

307
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:21,733
If he likes you,
you'll work here.

308
00:16:21,867 --> 00:16:23,267
We'll be together every day,
every night.

309
00:16:23,400 --> 00:16:25,000
You won't have to leave.

310
00:16:26,200 --> 00:16:27,267
Is that a promise?

311
00:16:27,833 --> 00:16:29,067
I promise.

312
00:16:30,633 --> 00:16:31,600
All right.

313
00:16:32,033 --> 00:16:33,267
Okay.

314
00:16:33,400 --> 00:16:34,833
I'll see you tomorrow.

315
00:16:35,467 --> 00:16:39,767
[BRAZEN MUSIC PLAYING]

316
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:43,567
<i> Okay, who else could it be?</i>

317
00:16:44,433 --> 00:16:49,733
You know, I'm sure it's Berdugo
who's meeting with Delilah.

318
00:16:51,767 --> 00:16:56,133
Okay, Joey, now we know when.

319
00:16:56,267 --> 00:16:59,667
What we need to know now
is where.

320
00:17:01,533 --> 00:17:03,467
What if...
[DAUNTING MUSIC PLAYING]

321
00:17:04,433 --> 00:17:06,167
We ambush Delilah tomorrow

322
00:17:06,300 --> 00:17:08,133
to have breakfast with us?

323
00:17:08,867 --> 00:17:09,933
That could work.

324
00:17:10,067 --> 00:17:11,200
Right?

325
00:17:11,333 --> 00:17:13,133
Or we could just follow her.

326
00:17:14,400 --> 00:17:16,333
But it's Berdugo.

327
00:17:16,467 --> 00:17:17,533
It's dangerous.

328
00:17:17,667 --> 00:17:21,033
I'm sure his men are armed.

329
00:17:22,267 --> 00:17:23,767
Could be.

330
00:17:30,967 --> 00:17:33,233
I thought you weren't mad at me
anymore?

331
00:17:35,333 --> 00:17:37,700
Why do you seem uninterested?

332
00:17:38,900 --> 00:17:40,467
No, I'm just sleepy.

333
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:42,133
[DREAMY MUSIC PLAYING]

334
00:17:42,267 --> 00:17:44,100
Sorry, I'm really tired.

335
00:17:45,100 --> 00:17:47,433
Can we talk about this
tomorrow instead?

336
00:17:47,567 --> 00:17:48,700
We still have plenty of time.

337
00:17:48,867 --> 00:17:50,200
I'm really sleepy.

338
00:17:50,333 --> 00:17:51,333
Of course.

339
00:17:52,667 --> 00:17:54,267
Stay on the bed.

340
00:17:55,767 --> 00:17:56,900
No, I won't.

341
00:17:57,033 --> 00:17:58,267
You paid for this, right?

342
00:17:58,400 --> 00:18:01,300
And you've already done so much
for our mission.

343
00:18:01,433 --> 00:18:03,200
I'm fine on the sofa.

344
00:18:03,333 --> 00:18:04,700
- I even prefer it.
- No, it's okay.

345
00:18:04,833 --> 00:18:07,500
No, it's just the right size
for me, see?

346
00:18:07,633 --> 00:18:11,667
[DREAMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

347
00:18:14,200 --> 00:18:15,100
Good night.

348
00:18:20,333 --> 00:18:28,133
[DREAMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

349
00:18:35,200 --> 00:18:37,900
[BREATHES]

350
00:18:38,033 --> 00:18:39,233
[SIGHS]

351
00:18:39,367 --> 00:18:43,367
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

352
00:18:46,300 --> 00:18:50,467
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

353
00:19:07,933 --> 00:19:12,133
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

354
00:19:22,867 --> 00:19:24,400
[DOOR CLOSING]

355
00:19:24,533 --> 00:19:28,867
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

356
00:19:34,567 --> 00:19:37,667
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

357
00:20:00,667 --> 00:20:02,133
[PHONE BEEPS]

358
00:20:02,300 --> 00:20:12,267
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

359
00:20:16,333 --> 00:20:18,967
<i>- Wow, it's beautiful here!
- It's beautiful, isn't it?</i>

360
00:20:19,100 --> 00:20:20,067
<i> Of course.</i>

361
00:20:20,200 --> 00:20:21,433
<i>- Oh, wait.
- Yes?</i>

362
00:20:21,567 --> 00:20:23,733
<i>- Let's take a picture.
- Okay, okay.</i>

363
00:20:23,867 --> 00:20:25,267
<i> Smile.</i>

364
00:20:26,333 --> 00:20:27,567
[CAMERA SHUTTER SNAPS]

365
00:20:32,767 --> 00:20:33,833
Why am I hurting?

366
00:20:33,967 --> 00:20:36,000
We're not even together.

367
00:20:44,067 --> 00:20:46,000
[EXHALES]

368
00:20:46,133 --> 00:20:50,133
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

369
00:20:59,267 --> 00:21:01,967
<i>That's why I want you back,
Andrew.</i>

370
00:21:02,100 --> 00:21:06,100
[STIRRING EMOTIONAL
MUSIC PLAYING]

371
00:21:09,900 --> 00:21:11,800
Why am I affected?

372
00:21:11,933 --> 00:21:15,900
[STIRRING EMOTIONAL
MUSIC CONTINUES]

373
00:21:21,300 --> 00:21:22,767
I don't want you anymore.

374
00:21:27,133 --> 00:21:30,433
Will I really be happy
if we get back together?

375
00:21:34,200 --> 00:21:38,267
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

376
00:21:49,533 --> 00:21:53,767
[STIRRING EMOTIONAL MUSIC
CONTINUES]

377
00:21:56,967 --> 00:21:59,600
<i>You don't know how.
Admit it!</i>

378
00:21:59,733 --> 00:22:00,933
<i> This is how it should be.</i>

379
00:22:01,067 --> 00:22:03,367
<i> Then like this, see?</i>

380
00:22:03,500 --> 00:22:05,900
[STIRRING EMOTIONAL MUSIC
PLAYING]

381
00:22:06,033 --> 00:22:09,200
[SPLASHES]

382
00:22:11,700 --> 00:22:15,833
[STIRRING EMOTIONAL MUSIC
CONTINUES]

383
00:22:22,133 --> 00:22:25,300
Now I know
what will make me happy.

384
00:22:26,567 --> 00:22:30,633
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

385
00:22:33,567 --> 00:22:35,300
You, young people...

386
00:22:35,433 --> 00:22:37,433
when you're not picked,
you think that's it,

387
00:22:37,567 --> 00:22:39,233
it's like the end of the world.

388
00:22:39,367 --> 00:22:40,833
I'll forget too.

389
00:22:40,967 --> 00:22:41,867
That's not true.

390
00:22:42,000 --> 00:22:43,000
Ma'am Delilah is expecting

391
00:22:43,133 --> 00:22:44,167
- your arrival.
- Make sure...

392
00:22:44,300 --> 00:22:45,700
nothing will go wrong tomorrow,
okay?

393
00:22:45,833 --> 00:22:48,300
If something goes wrong
with this deal,

394
00:22:48,467 --> 00:22:51,600
your Lumen-X will be history
in Valmora.

395
00:22:51,733 --> 00:22:53,100
You are just a distributor.

396
00:22:53,233 --> 00:22:55,200
Don't get too comfortable.

397
00:22:55,333 --> 00:22:56,700
I'm not above hitting a woman!

398
00:22:56,833 --> 00:22:58,667
What's going on with Sir Tomas?

399
00:22:58,800 --> 00:23:00,600
No matter what he promises you,

400
00:23:00,733 --> 00:23:02,633
do not take it.

401
00:23:02,767 --> 00:23:03,633
Have you told him yet?

402
00:23:03,767 --> 00:23:06,133
Dad, mom isn't here right now.

403
00:23:06,267 --> 00:23:07,867
Joey, your father is alive?
